  "flight": {
    "notes": "Tuning values from approximate public Su-25 figures: two R-95Sh turbojets of 40.2 kN each without afterburner, less installation losses (about 5%), lapsing as the F-21's engine does at military power; wing 30.1 m2, span 14.36 m; inertias scaled from the F-16's by mass and span, the wing's stations and tip pods adding roll inertia. The standard load is two short-range missiles, ten pylons, 250 rounds and the pilot, with the armor in the empty mass. A straight, thick wing: k for aspect ratio 6.85 and Oswald efficiency 0.8, drag divergence near Mach 0.75, the stall near 20 deg; big flaps with the gear. The speedbrakes split the wingtip pods. Angles in degrees, everything else SI.",
